              <span class="case-hero__title-accent">Particle Text.</span>
              <span class="case-hero__title-muted">A WebGL playground for breaking<br />SVG shapes into motion.</span>
            </h1>
          </div>

          <div class="case-hero__grid">
            <div class="type-heading-lg case-hero__summary">
              <p>
                A small experiment where thousands of points are sampled from an SVG silhouette and simulated in 3D with Three.js. The default shape, Break the Shape, becomes a responsive field of particles: it can be pushed by the cursor, spread through scroll, hit by radial waves, and scattered by click explosions before finding its way back.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a class="case-hero__link" href="https://github.com/Puschkarew/ParticleText">github.com/Puschkarew/ParticleText</a>
              </p>
            </div>
